         recommended test: A test is added that verifies an obligation whose quotation lies within its attributed requirement span remains attributed to that requirement.
           inputs:  Construct a task file with at least two requirements whose text overlaps enough that one obligation’s quotation appears inside both spans, but attribute that obligation to the requirement whose own span already contains the quotation. The key input characteristic is a same-requirement match that is also a plausible cross-requirement match, so a buggy implementation that always re-files by span containment will change the owning requirement even though the correct implementation must not.
           detects: A developer always re-files an obligation to the requirement whose span contains its quotation, even when that is the same requirement it was originally attributed to.
           full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion test-obligation-keeps-own-span

